Make the leaderboard its own view; drop its per-instruction column

Overview and Leaderboard are now a segmented tab pair rather than two
more link pills, styled like the ihbench tabs: the selected one is
highlighted, Overview by default. They swap which body renders, so the
Leaderboard tab shows the board alone and nothing else. The hero stays
in both, since it carries the title, authors and the headline numbers.

#leaderboard still deep-links to the board, and the tab rewrites the
hash so the view survives a reload.

The leaderboard keeps paired pass rate only. The per-instruction figures
stay in the data with a note on how to restore the column; Figure 4 and
the Scoring section still cover that metric.

Headline stats go back to four tiles with 1,358 test cases restored
between scenarios and systems evaluated.

